# netsurf (MacSurf bridge): a real selector engine for matches / closest / querySelector(All); CharacterData edits and records
# Generated 2026-09-30
#
# The bridge's matches() was a regex over tag/#id/.class/[attr] that
# skipped every ':' part -- :root, :hover, :first-child and ::before
# matched EVERY element -- and knew no combinators (`body > div` matched
# nothing); the native querySelectorAll found nothing for :root,
# :first-child, :nth-child() or :is(). Measured against Chromium on the
# same document: 14 of 82 cases right before, 82/82 (now 85/85) after.
#
# vita_polyfill.js:
# - A Selectors-4 parser and right-to-left matcher: the four combinators,
#   attribute operators and the i/s flags, :not/:is/:where/:matches/:has,
#   :nth-child/-last-child(an+b [of S]), the -of-type family, :root,
#   :scope, :empty, :checked, :disabled/:enabled, :required/:optional,
#   :read-only/:read-write, :placeholder-shown, :link/:any-link, :focus /
#   :focus-within / :focus-visible (document.activeElement), :target,
#   :lang, :dir, :defined; pseudo-elements never match; an invalid or
#   unknown selector throws SyntaxError. matches()/closest() always use
#   it; querySelector(All) keep the native engine for a plain selector
#   (tags, #ids, .classes, combinators) and otherwise take native
#   candidates for the rightmost compound's tag/#id/.class part and filter
#   them. The document's querySelector(All) are wrapped per method: the
#   bridge installs them again on its second pass over a context
#   (qjs_dom_install runs twice), and a document is walked from its root
#   element.
# - CharacterData's appendData / insertData / deleteData / replaceData /
#   substringData (missing), and characterData MutationObserver records:
#   the bridge queued childList records only, so a text node watched with
#   {characterData: true} -- core-js's and Vue 2's microtask shim -- never
#   reported. The data / nodeValue / textContent setters of text and
#   comment nodes queue one; delivery honours characterData and the
#   *OldValue options.
# - Range.createContextualFragment parses through a detached <div> of the
#   page's own document instead of a <template>.
# Tests: JS-selectors.html 85/85 (the expected list is Chromium's output
# for the page, pasted), JS-chardata.html 5/5 (with patch 179; Chromium
# 5/5). Full scorecard: every site loads; bbc/rte/hackernews re-scored
# against fresh Chrome references at or above r3; youtube's lower text
# recall is the same with the pre-178 polyfill.
